overview: live window previews with keyboard and mouse selection

Replaces the preview-all-windows patch (dwm-preview-all-windows-6.5.diff)
with a reworked implementation of the same idea:

- overview {.i = 0}: visible clients of the selected monitor
  overview {.i = 1}: all clients on all monitors, grouped by tag and
  labelled "<tag>: <title>"
- live previews: XComposite window pixmaps scaled by XRender (bilinear),
  refreshed at overviewfps; works with or without a compositor
- Tab/Shift+Tab, arrows, hjkl or the scroll wheel select, hovering
  selects, Return/Space/Button1 jump to the client (switching monitor
  and tag if needed), Escape/Button3 cancel; pressing the overview
  binding again cycles
- keeps handling X events while open (new/closed clients rebuild the grid)
- overlay windows have WM_CLASS "dwm-overview" for compositor rules

Needs -lXcomposite -lXrender (already in config.mk via preview-all-windows).

